From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 20:31:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 524/524] [DS4.1] PDL: DeepSeek's TileKernels switch only for
 the chain's own calls

The source check over the kernel tests (dgx4, 2026-10-25) found TileKernels
kernels that read an input before their wait when PDL is on: the mHC post
reads its mixes, RoPE its positions and cos/sin table (and waits inside a
branch). DeepSeek's placement is safe only where the kernel launched just
before them did not write those inputs. The deployment never launches them,
but set_pdl(True) at first use turned PDL on for every TileKernels kernel,
the tests' references included.

pdl.per_token_cast, pdl.norm_forward and pdl.moe_topk_gate_forward now set
the switch for their call only and restore it: the casts, norms and top-k
gate on the decode chain, which wait first. Every other TileKernels kernel
keeps its default (no PDL).

Tests: the early reader is its own kernel (pdl_early_reader), which the
source check exempts by name; a cast through pdl has a programmatic edge in
a captured graph and a direct TileKernels call does not; the switch is off
after either. The layer chain casts through pdl when the build has it.
